Slices 1 and 2 are both on `main` (`e9fd862`), reviewed and approved, and every check passes on the merged tree. It finished at 12:30 UTC, ahead of my estimate. Nothing was pushed.

**What's on `main` now:**
- **Duel core (slice 1):**
  - a deterministic integer 1v1 fight simulation (Duelist kit, guard levels, throws, stamina, combo scaling, KO and timeout);
  - rollback snapshots and replay;
  - keyboard throw input fixed (see below).
- **Sea (slice 2):**
  - a Tiled-authored map with four islands, shoals and docks;
  - sailing with acceleration, braking and turning;
  - docking;
  - server-side visibility, so a client never receives ships out of sight (tested down to the raw network bytes);
  - a client map with camera and a fogged minimap.
- **Final checks on the merged tree:** 271 unit tests, 21 integration tests and 4/4 browser scenarios passed. Typecheck and build passed, and the build step now loads 8 exports from `dist/`, including the duel ones.

**How it got there (5 runs):**

| Run | Result |
|---|---|
| `duel-core-001` | Challenge paused once; I revised the plan. Approved. |
| `duel-core-fixes-001` | Approved. Fixed two P1 bugs that my review subagent found and **both official reviewers missed**: a keyboard throw (J then K a frame apart) always became a jab, and a strike that missed still cancelled a throw. |
| `world-sea-001` | Blocked by the coverage reviewer: nothing tested that the map is actually drawn. The general reviewer never gave a verdict. |
| `world-sea-fixes-001` | Restored that snapshot, added real pixel tests for terrain and fog plus six smaller fixes. Approved with a full review. |

**Key decisions I made while you slept:**
1. **Build proof for the duel code:** each package checks its own new export after building (`postbuild`), because the shared smoke script belonged to the other run. Once both were merged I added the duel exports to the smoke script (`e9fd862`).
2. **Replay runner:** it lives in `simulation/duel` for now rather than `test-tools`, to avoid touching the other run's lockfile.
3. **Duel rules the spec leaves open:**
   - all same-frame hits are resolved together;
   - two throws on the same frame cancel each other;
   - a strike beats a throw only if it actually connects;
   - a guard break *adds* 30 stamina.
4. **Throw input:** a just-started jab or heavy converts into a throw if the other button arrives within 1–2 frames. I chose this over delaying lone buttons because it keeps the spec's jab startup of 7 frames.
5. **Follow-up features instead of hand edits:** review findings went through their own workflow runs rather than me editing reviewed code. For the world follow-up, reviewers saw the whole feature again, because no general review had ever covered it.
6. **Merges into `main`:** duel by fast-forward, world by a merge commit. I checked beforehand that the merge was conflict-free and that the merged tests passed.

**Needs your attention:**
- **The sea map is 99.2% empty** (224×208 tiles). Ships kept the skeleton's speed, so islands had to be far apart to meet the 20–40 s travel targets. With a 10-tile sight radius, players will rarely see each other. Decide on faster ships or a denser map before the encounters slice.
- **Small open items, none blocking:**
  - an edge case in the throw-window validation;
  - duel types lost `readonly`;
  - partial range tests for `restoreDuel`;
  - a hard-coded env var name in the smoke script;
  - `docs/architecture.md` doesn't list the duel packages yet (`docs/duel.md` covers them).
- **Cleanup when convenient:** 6 `feature/*` branches plus `skeleton/candidate-001` and `world/base`, the `~/dev/project-B-world` worktree, and old run workspaces.

The full timeline, reviews and all 13 logged decisions are in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-agentops-dev-project-B/0094b893-59da-46a6-a9fa-4f48e374f4db/scratchpad/slices-1-2-review.md`.

